    "created_at": "2016-03-16T10:27:21Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-03-16T10:27:21Z",
    "body": "So http://heycam.github.io/webidl/#SameObject doesn't really do anything and just serves as documentation AFAICT, and in Blink the extended attribute has no effect. I guess it should allow for optimizations in bindings, but if it's used like that it won't make sense for `ancestorOrigins`.\n\nSo... should we drop `[SameObject]` in this case? The spec now defines the behavior in prose.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
